	(text "5 V → 3.3 V regulator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 62.23 68.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aaa429f9-7894-4260-8aa4-5e8c66974880")
	)
	(text "1. Supply input\n   • +5V from the carrier on M.2 pins 20/22 (4.75–5.25 V, max 5.5 V). The carrier supplies\n     +5V only; +3V3 is generated here and is never tied to a carrier rail.\n   • D2 SMF6.0A TVS (VRWM 6 V > 5.25 V max; IR ≤ 400 µA at 6 V, far less at 5 V; VC 10.3 V; 200 W;\n     unidirectional: cathode → +5V) clamps spikes on +5V and conducts negative transients to GND.\n     At a 10.3 V clamp: U2 18 V abs, C1 25 V, C10 16 V, Q1/Q2/Q4 40 V, Q3 30 V: safe; PB2 sees\n     10.3 V × 10k / 30k = 3.43 V via R8/R9: PB2 is FT_ea (VDD + 4 V max), R8 limits < 0.35 mA.\n   • C1 10 µF/25 V 0805 (≈ 5 µF at 5 V bias) + C10 100 nF at U2 IN.\n\n2. 3.3 V LDO — U2 TI TLV76733DRVR: VIN 2.5–16 V (18 V abs), 1 A, thermal shutdown 180 °C,\n   fold-back current limit, stable with ≥ 1 µF ceramic, WSON-6 2 × 2 mm (RθJA 77.7 °C/W).\n   EN → IN (always on), SNS → OUT, thermal pad → GND.\n   Worst-case 3V3 load:\n     STM32G0B1 @ 64 MHz, all peripherals ......... 20 mA\n     SN65HVD230 dominant into the 60 Ω bus ....... 67 mA  (17 mA no-load + VOD 3 V / 60 Ω;\n                                                           ≈ 17 mA RMS in normal traffic, TI Fig. 1)\n     X1 8 MHz oscillator (Icc max) ............... 10 mA\n     GPIO + Q4 base drive ........................  1 mA\n     Module subtotal ............................. 98 mA\n     Carrier allowance (M.2 pin 4, ≤ 50 mA) ...... 50 mA\n     TOTAL ...................................... 148 mA   (15 % of the 1 A rating)\n   Dropout: 1.4 V max @ 1 A (≈ 1.4 Ω) → ≈ 0.2 V @ 148 mA → needs VIN ≥ 3.5 V  ≪  4.75 V OK\n   Dissipation: P = (5.25 − 3.3) V × 148 mA = 0.29 W → ΔT = 0.29 W × 77.7 °C/W ≈ 22 °C\n     Module rated −20…+70 °C ambient: TJ = 70 + 22 = 92 °C ≤ 125 °C OK.\n     A short on pin 4 / TP2 is caught by the fold-back limit + thermal shutdown.\n     PCB: thermal pad → top GND copper → vias beside it (none in the pad).\n   Output: C2 10 µF/25 V 0805 (≈ 6.9 µF at 3.3 V; TLV767 needs ≥ 0.5 µF effective) + C3 100 nF;\n     C4/C5 at the MCU (MCU sheet).\n\n3. Power indicator LEDs     I = (Vsupply − Vf) / R\n   LED1 red   (+5V present): (5.0 − 2.0) / 1 kΩ = 3.0 mA\n   LED2 green (3V3 present): green Vf ≈ 2.8 V is too high to run bright from 3.3 V, so LED2 is fed\n     from +5V and switched by Q4, whose base (R13 10k) is driven by +3V3. It lights once 3V3 is\n     above ≈ 1 V: a 'rail present' indicator, not a 'rail in regulation' check.\n     I = (5.0 − 2.8 − 0.1 VCE(sat)) / 1 kΩ ≈ 2.1 mA;  base (3.3 − 0.7) / 10 kΩ = 0.26 mA\n   All 4 LEDs: 0805, JLC Basic parts, 4 different colours.\n\n4. Status LEDs — +5V supply, MMBT3904 low-side (white Vf ≈ 2.8 V is too high for 3.3 V)\n   LED3 white : (5.0 − 2.8 − 0.1 VCE(sat)) / 1 kΩ ≈ 2.1 mA   (CAN status)\n   LED4 yellow: (5.0 − 2.0 − 0.1) / 1 kΩ ≈ 2.9 mA   (user GPIO)\n   Base: (3.3 − 0.7) / 10 kΩ = 0.26 mA → IC/IB ≈ 8 (LED3), 11 (LED4) ≪ hFE ≥ 100 → saturated\n   CAN_LED = PB4, USER_LED = PB5, GPIO high = LED on.\n\n5. 5 V input monitor — R8 20k / R9 10k / C9 → PB2 (ADC1_IN10)\n   VSENSE = 5.0 × 10k / (20k + 10k) = 1.67 V      full scale = 3 × VDDA = 9.9 V\n   Source impedance 20k ∥ 10k = 6.7 kΩ (< 50 kΩ ADC limit) → sampling time ≥ 39.5 cycles\n   Firmware: VDDA = 3.0 V × VREFINT_CAL / VREFINT_DATA\n             V(+5V) = ADC / 4095 × VDDA × 3\n   Tip: sample with BZ1 silent (its current steps ripple +5V) or average several readings.\n\n6. Buzzer — BZ1 KLJ-5018-5040 PASSIVE magnetic buzzer (no oscillator inside): 5 V (4–6 V),\n   25 ± 3 Ω coil, ≥ 90 dB @ 10 cm, ≤ 80 mA mean at 4 kHz / 50 % duty; 5.5 × 5.5 × 1.8 mm.\n   PB7 = TIM4_CH2 PWM, 4 kHz: PSC 0, ARR 15999, CCR2 8000 (50 %). Lower duty = quieter.\n   End each tone with CCR2 = 0 (PB7 LOW). Never DC HIGH: 5 V / 25 Ω = 200 mA = 1 W in the coil.\n   Q3 AO3400A low-side (≤ 48 mΩ at VGS 2.5 V); D3 carries the coil current in each PWM off-time.\n   R12 4.7k keeps Q3 off in reset/boot even if a weak internal pull-up (≥ 25 kΩ) is on PB7:\n   VGS ≤ 3.3 × 4.7 / 29.7 = 0.52 V < 0.65 V (AO3400A VGS(th) min).\n\n7. Test points (top side, 1 mm pads): TP1 +5V, TP2 +3V3, TP3 GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.855 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ddf3b2c5-5bf5-4732-91c4-2605ce338c06")
	)
	(text "Buzzer (KLJ-5018-5040 passive, PWM)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
